# .public-surface-allow - justified exceptions to scripts/public-surface-check.
#
#     category | path-glob | reason | pattern
#
#   category    a deny category (see `scripts/public-surface-check --help`) or
#               `*` for every category
#   path-glob   `*` for the whole repository, a glob over the repository
#               relative path, or `COMMIT` for commit-message exceptions
#   reason      required, at least 8 characters: why the text is legitimately
#               public, not what the pattern does
#   pattern     POSIX ERE, with %HH hex escapes so a term can be named without
#               being spelled
#
# This repository needs no exceptions today, and that is worth recording,
# because an earlier audit floated two candidates that turn out not to need a
# rule. Do not add one for them:
#
#   * the `ghp_xxx` placeholders in README.md and testdata/. A provider token
#     is only reported with a full-length body after the prefix, so an obvious
#     placeholder in a config example is not a finding.
#   * the `/home/user/...` paths in service_test.go. A home directory is not a
#     deny category; only private hosts, cluster shapes and secret stores are.
#
# Both stay quiet because the deny patterns are narrow, not because anything
# excuses them. Widening the allowlist to cover them would switch off a check
# that is currently doing its job. Add a rule only for text this guard actually
# reports, and say in the reason why publishing it is intended.
